WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.330
A train waits at a platform.

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:06.360
On its smooth floor sits
a ball, perfectly still.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.990
The train pulls away, speeding up.

4
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.820
Nobody touches the ball.

5
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.190
Nothing pushes it.

6
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.180
Yet a passenger sees the ball start
rolling to the back of the train,

7
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.280
faster and faster.

8
00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:23.350
Newton's first law says an object keeps
its velocity unless a net force acts on

9
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:23.930
it.

10
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.350
So is the law broken here?

11
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.350
In this mission, you'll ask
who is watching the ball,

12
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.710
and from where.

13
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.910
Then you'll look at passengers
in three moving vehicles,

14
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.570
and decide what each of
them should conclude.

15
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:41.480
Your mission: decide whether Newton's
first law really breaks down on the train.
